  "_about": "Shared recurrence fixtures for pytest (backend/tests/unit/test_recurrence.py) and flutter test (app/test/features/calendar/domain/rrule_spec_test.dart). Semantics are defined in docs/api/contract.md section 5. valid[]: 'input' must be accepted and canonicalized to 'canonical' (canonical is a fixed point). For timed cases (all_day=false) 'dtstart_local' is the wall-clock start in 'tz' and 'expected_local' lists occurrence starts as wall-clock times in 'tz' whose start lies in [range[0] 00:00, range[1] 00:00) in 'tz'; 'expected_utc' is the same list as UTC instants. expected_local is the nominal wall-clock time the rule generates: inside a spring-forward gap it does not exist, and expected_utc shows how it resolves (PEP 495 fold=0, the offset before the transition; contract section 5.3), so do not derive expected_local by converting expected_utc back to local time. For all-day cases dtstart_local and expected_local are floating dates (YYYY-MM-DD) and the range is [range[0], range[1]) in dates; tz is ignored. invalid[]: must be rejected with 422 code 'invalid_rrule' and errors[0].type equal to the case's 'reason'; each case has exactly one defect; 'start_date' is the event's local start date (timed events start at 19:00 local in Europe/Bucharest). birthdays[]: yearly birthday expansion (member birthdays when start_date is null, kind=birthday events otherwise); Feb 29 falls on Feb 28 in non-leap years.",
